course: dictionary
lesson: 5229
title: Same word, different meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the words around them tell you which one the writer means. Jerry is a good example. It can be a name, a can for carrying fuel or water, or a mouse in a cartoon. Ask yourself what would fit in the sentence, then try your meaning and check that it still makes sense.
explain: «Fill the jerry can with water before we go camping.» The words fill, water and camping show that a jerry can is a container, not a person. «Jerry is my best friend at school.» Here Jerry is a name, because a best friend is a person. Capital letters help too, but the sentence matters most.
explain: «In every episode of Tom and Jerry a grey cat crashes round a big kitchen after a cheeky mouse» tells you that Jerry is the mouse. The words cat, kitchen and mouse are the clues. Always read the whole sentence before you decide what a word means.
fact: Jerry is a boy's or man's name, often short for Gerald or Jeremy.
fact: A jerry can is a flat metal or plastic can for carrying fuel or water.
fact: Jerry is the mouse in the cartoon «Tom and Jerry».
fact: Petrol must be kept away from fire, so a jerry can holding petrol needs careful handling.
fact: One word can have several meanings; the context shows you which one fits.
exercise: «Fill the jerry can with water before we go camping.» What is a jerry can? | A kind of cat | A cartoon mouse | A boy's name | *A flat metal or plastic can for carrying water
exercise: «Jerry is my best friend at school.» What kind of word is Jerry here? | A type of cat | *A person's name | A mouse | A can for petrol
exercise: Which character is Jerry in «Tom and Jerry»? | A cartoon fox | A cartoon bear | A grey cat | *A cheeky mouse
test: «Keep the jerry can away from the fire.» Why must you be careful? | Fire keeps petrol cool | Cans are always full of sweets | Jerry cans are painted pink | *Petrol must be kept away from fire
test: «Tom chases Jerry around the kitchen.» What is Jerry in this sentence? | A can of petrol | *A mouse | A type of cat | A boy in the kitchen
exam: «Jerry filled the jerry can with petrol for the car.» What does the first Jerry mean? | *A person's name | A mouse | A cartoon | A kind of fuel
